  m_Name: CaptainsCabin
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  Name: B5 - Captain's Cabin
  Text: The control cabins of the R-rigid airships featured advanced systems for
    their time. They included helm and rudder controls for steering, along with gas
    and ballast systems to manage altitude. Navigation instruments like compasses,
    altimeters, and barometers guided the crew, while engine control stations oversaw
    the airship's multiple engines. Communication relied on speaking tubes and signals
    to coordinate operations. The cabins prioritized efficiency and safety, reflecting
    the innovative design of early airship engineering. These elements showcased
    the ambition and ingenuity of the era's aeronautical technology.
